  "articleSummary": "**Summary:**  \nThe article argues that AI agents are useless without integration into real business systems (Salesforce, Jira, etc.) and that the Model Context Protocol (MCP) solves this by standardizing tool connections—like USB-C for AI integrations. It positions MCP as an alternative to writing custom API wrappers for each service, enabling agents to access multiple tools through a single protocol. Using Mastra’s `MCPClient`, the article provides a tutorial-style walkthrough for setting up local and remote integrations, handling per-user authentication, and avoiding hardcoded credentials in production. The tone is analytical and instructional, framed around the recurring metaphor of MCP as a universal connector that eliminates the “drawer full of cables” problem.  \n*Intended audience:* Developers building and deploying AI agents.",
